## swift-rs and SwiftRs

Two independently resolved components are recorded:

1. The Rust `swift-rs` crate, version 1.0.8, copied to `vendor/swift-rs`. The local build compatibility patch detects modern SwiftPM static archive output and restores only the explicitly declared `retain_object` / `release_object` exports in Mado's embedded `SwiftRs.o`, retaining the unique-definition guard. Required `llvm-objcopy` failures stop the build. Runtime function implementations are unchanged; `vendor/README.md` records the scope and build-tool prerequisite. Original [MIT](docs/licenses/rust/swift-rs-1.0.8/LICENSE-MIT) and [Apache-2.0](docs/licenses/rust/swift-rs-1.0.8/LICENSE-APACHE) texts are retained.
2. The SwiftPM `SwiftRs` component fetched by mado, pinned to `e0b4a5f444a4204efa8e8270468318bc7836fcce` in `brendonovich/swift-rs`. Its [MIT](docs/licenses/swift-rs-e0b4a5f444a4204efa8e8270468318bc7836fcce/LICENSE-MIT) and [Apache-2.0](docs/licenses/swift-rs-e0b4a5f444a4204efa8e8270468318bc7836fcce/LICENSE-APACHE) texts were copied from the actual SwiftPM checkout.

Both declare `MIT OR Apache-2.0`; neither is relabeled as solely MIT. The MIT copyright is `Copyright (c) 2023 The swift-rs Developers`.

